From: pocket_vm developers <pocket-vm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] um: drop the free_irqs() call from the SIGIO handler

_sigio_handler() runs as a signal handler, so it must not call anything that
can sleep. free_irqs() reaches the generic free_irq(), and on a CONFIG_SMP=y
kernel __synchronize_irq() gets there to synchronize_irqwork(), whose
irq_work_sync() waits on an rcuwait and then calls synchronize_rcu(). Tree RCU
blocks, so schedule() runs from the interrupted, frequently idle, task inside
an interrupt and produces "bad: scheduling from the idle thread!", runqueue and
RCU corruption and a kernel fault. A uniprocessor kernel survives only because
Tiny RCU and the UP synchronize_irqwork() stub never block.

Remove the call. The following patch moves the drain into process context; a
channel queued between these two patches is simply freed on the next drain.
---
 arch/um/kernel/irq.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/um/kernel/irq.c b/arch/um/kernel/irq.c
index ddfd6e9bd8c7..f421e2ed23f0 100644
--- a/arch/um/kernel/irq.c
+++ b/arch/um/kernel/irq.c
@@ -234,9 +234,6 @@ static void _sigio_handler(struct uml_pt_regs *regs,
 						  timetravel_handlers_only);
 		}
 	}
-
-	if (!timetravel_handlers_only)
-		free_irqs();
 }
 
 void sigio_handler(int sig, struct siginfo *unused_si, struct uml_pt_regs *regs,
-- 
